        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-0 gap-x-10 min-[860px]:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr]">
          <FaqItem q={"Can I apply for a Bhutan visa myself?"} open><p>No — international tourist visas must be lodged by a licensed Bhutanese tour operator as part of a booked itinerary. There's no independent or walk-in visa application process for international visitors.</p></FaqItem>
          <FaqItem q={"Is the SDF the same as the visa fee?"}><p>No, they're separate. The visa application fee is a one-time US$40 charge; the SDF is a nightly fee (US$100 for most international adults) charged for every night of your stay. Both are included in your Marvels Luxe quote.</p></FaqItem>
          <FaqItem q={"Can I enter and exit through different border points?"}><p>Yes — some travelers fly into Paro and depart overland through Phuentsholing, or the reverse, especially when combining Bhutan with a trip to India. Tell us if you'd like to plan it that way.</p></FaqItem>
        </div>
